# File: tests/features/add_greeting_nfkc_library_helper.feature
# Generated from: specs/356-add-greeting-nfkc-library-helper/requirements.md
Feature: Return the completed greeting in Unicode NFKC

  @SCN001
  Scenario: Replace compatibility characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkc is called with U+FB01 ona, full-width Ada, and Ada no-break-space Lovelace
    Then the results are Hello, fiona with 12 code points, then Hello, Ada with 10 code points, then Hello, Ada Lovelace with 19 code points
    And each result is a str

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Compose decomposed characters
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkc is called with Chloe plus U+0301
    Then the result is Hello, precomposed Chloé with 12 code points

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Leave already-normalized text unchanged
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkc is called with Ada, Ada two-spaces Lovelace, and O'Brien-Smith
    Then each result equals greet of the same name

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Agree with unicodedata NFKC
    Given the installed nmg_sdlc_smoke package
    When greeting_nfkc is called with Ada, Chloe plus U+0301, U+FB01 ona, and O'Brien-Smith
    Then each result equals unicodedata NFKC normalization of greet of the same name
    And each result is NFKC-normalized

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Preserve invalid-name behavior
    Given the invalid names empty, space-tab, None, and 42
    When greeting_nfkc is called with each invalid name
    Then each call raises ValueError with message name must not be blank

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Expose and document the helper
    Given the README Library section
    When the README Library example runs and prints greeting_nfkc of U+FB01 ona
    Then it prints Hello, fiona and greeting_nfkc is listed in nmg_sdlc_smoke.__all__
    And the README documents the NFKC rule and the inherited invalid-name error
